{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161955-gnosis-and-archmastery","id":1161955,"title":"Gnosis and Archmastery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-23T13:46:31-08:00","id":1161955,"title":"Gnosis and Archmastery","content":"I am under the impression that Gnosis higher than 5 is the territory of Archmasters and supposed to be pretty rare. Am I wrong in tis regard? I cannot find anything in the books to confirm or deny it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T13:53:27-08:00","id":1161958,"title":"","content":"Gnosis 6+ is necessary for Archmastery, but Archmastery is not necessary for Gnosis 6+. Given the difficulty and trials involved in a Threshold Seeking to become an Archmaster, the former is more common than the latter (which is not the same as saying it's common).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T16:54:41-08:00","id":1162012,"title":"","content":"Gnosis 6 is explicitly mentioned at some point as being the <i>easiest to achieve</i> prerequisite for Archmastery. Gnosis 6+ is not the territory of Archmasters: it's where you need to be if you even want to <i>start</i> trying to become an Archmaster.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 6 Mages are probably much more common than Archmasters: every Mage who Masters both of his Ruling Arcana needs to have Gnosis at 6, for example, so I imagine there are at least a few of those in most Caucuses and Consilii.<br /> <br /> IIRC, a Gnosis 6+ Mage who wants to decide to become an Archmaster then needs to decouple themselves from Caucus, Consilium, and general Pentacle politics, build up enough magical knowledge and experience chasing Archmastery (i.e. build up enough XP to <i>buy</i> the sixth dot in an Arcanum), and then figure out how to actually do the Threshold Seeking trial to become an Archmaster.<br /> <br /> Few powerful Mages are willing to give up everything they've accomplished so far to chase the Imperial Mysteries, and fewer succeed at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T17:37:50-08:00","id":1162020,"title":"","content":"It's lonely at the top.<br /> <br /> You almost become inhuman as you progress from Gnosis 6. Your Nimbus infects practically everything around you. Your Paradox dice for over-Reaching can become dangerously large. You are driven by Obsession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-23-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T19:41:34-08:00","id":1162326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161955-gnosis-and-archmastery?p=1162020#post1162020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's lonely at the top.<br /> <br /> You almost become inhuman as you progress from Gnosis 6. Your Nimbus infects practically everything around you. Your Paradox dice for over-Reaching can become dangerously large. You are driven by Obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>and my gosh does all that make me salivate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}